<Layout title="Our Team" current="our-team" description="Nittany Rover Team’s founding mission and Penn State University Park’s documented participation in the inaugural 2007 University Rover Challenge.">
  <PageIntro title="Nittany Rover Team" />
  <section class="container article-section split"><div><h2>Our purpose</h2></div><div><p>The Nittany Rover Team brings together Penn State University Park students with a shared ambition to advance space robotics. Our goal is to turn classroom knowledge and individual experience into collaborative engineering work that prepares members for careers in space.</p><p>Through development, research, and competition, we aim to give students opportunities to design, build, test, and lead. We connect mechanical design, electronics, software, and science so members can learn across disciplines and tackle complex problems together.</p><p>We’re building an organization that can sustain ambitious projects across generations of students. By sharing knowledge, mentoring future leaders, and documenting our work, we aim to create a lasting community for space engineering at Penn State.</p></div></section>
  <section class="dark-section"><div class="container section split"><div class="year-block">2007<small>PENN STATE’S FIRST URC CHAPTER</small></div><div><h2>One of the original four</h2><p>Penn State University Park’s Mars Society participated in the inaugural University Rover Challenge alongside Brigham Young University, the University of California, Los Angeles, and the University of Nevada, Reno.</p><p>A contemporary October 2007 report describes the team’s trip to Utah, its rover, and equipment difficulties that prevented it from completing all of its tasks.</p><p>Nittany Rover Team’s founding effort builds on that early involvement, with a new project and a commitment to lasting participation.</p><p class="source-note"><a href={sources.history}>Read the October 22, 2007 report ↗</a></p></div></div></section>
  <section class="container section split"><h2>Join the founding team</h2><div><p>Relevant experience can come from research, internships, personal projects, fabrication, programming, electronics, or scientific work. We’re seeking students ready to contribute that experience to a founding team.</p><a class="button" href={href('join')}>Application information ↗</a></div></section>
</Layout>
